From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: punktfunk <packages@unom.io>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] pipewire: give a planar capture DRM LINEAR's layout on NVIDIA

A planar capture dmabuf came from a plain VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR image: no
modifier, no VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo, and STORAGE usage NV12 and P010
do not have. The driver promises nothing about that image, while a consumer
imports it as DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, which means pitch page kind. Page kind
sets the layout of bits in memory. On a pre-Turing NVIDIA GPU the kinds differ
and the consumer reads a picture with its address bits 5 to 9 permuted.

On NVIDIA, ask for what the consumer imports: the LINEAR modifier, external
memory, and the planes' R8/RG8 views listed with MUTABLE_FORMAT and
EXTENDED_USAGE, which is where the storage usage comes from. A driver that
cannot make that promise does not get the format offered, so the consumer
negotiates packed RGB. Other vendors keep the plain image.

punktfunk: also stamps the version banner +pfhdr32.
